{"id":1,"explanation":"The check in verify must reject a nonce already in seen; removing it would let a token be replayed. #123 is an issue reference for the warning.","unsure":""}
{"id":2,"explanation":"Run ensure_key_salt before constructing KeyManager. If ensuring the salt fails, abort startup instead of initializing the manager.","unsure":""}
{"id":3,"explanation":"The topN used to allocate buf must be no greater than maxSimpleTopN, and the resulting slice must stay within 1 MiB.","unsure":""}
{"id":4,"explanation":"When meta.abi_version is missing, abi must remain None. Treating the missing value as the current ABI would be unsafe. #1784 is an issue reference.","unsure":""}
{"id":5,"explanation":"The external TLP configuration at /etc/tlp.conf is read after files in /etc/tlp.d/, so its values override the drop-in written at /etc/tlp.d/90-power.conf.","unsure":""}
{"id":6,"explanation":"The set_key configuration assumes TLP version 1.10 or later. _AC, _BAT and _SAV are suffixes for profiles. Leaving an _AC setting unset preserves GNOME's Performance toggle; this code sets only the battery profile value.","unsure":"The comment does not expand the profile names, particularly _SAV."}
{"id":7,"explanation":"On a JSON parse error, return null so the caller can log a warning. Throwing from this catch block would bypass that intended handling.","unsure":""}
{"id":8,"explanation":"When AllowedTools is set, RemoveSkipPermissions must remove --dangerously-skip-permissions from the arguments. That flag would bypass the restrictions supplied through --allowedTools.","unsure":""}
{"id":9,"explanation":"For the dead-code decision made by thunk_is_dead, consult the verdict table associated with is_definitely_dead_code in rust/xray-core/src/compiler/graph_preamble.rs. The path and symbol are a code reference.","unsure":""}
{"id":10,"explanation":"Replace the fixed repos_skipped value with a count derived from the domains-to-repos mapping. #874 is the issue tracking that work.","unsure":""}
{"id":11,"explanation":"The regex_query call uses a linear-time DFA for matching, so its regex evaluation does not backtrack. This is the performance reason for using it here.","unsure":""}
{"id":12,"explanation":"Keep the refresh_tokens table definition in sync with RefreshTokenSqliteBackend._ensure_schema in src/storage/refresh_token_backend.py. The path and qualified name identify the corresponding schema code.","unsure":""}
{"id":13,"explanation":"MAX_BATCH is 500 because the vendor's batch API accepts at most 500 items. doc:vendor-api#limits points to the limits section of the vendor API documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":14,"explanation":"Keep these Status values in sync with STATUS_LABELS in web/src/status.ts. Their iota order determines stored integer values, so reordering them would change what existing integers mean. #88 is an issue reference.","unsure":""}
{"id":15,"explanation":"The index must list tenant_id before created_at to match the orders_by_tenant query. The comment identifies the query by name but gives no file path.","unsure":""}
{"id":16,"explanation":"TList.Add must preserve the rule that FCount never exceeds the length of FItems. Grow is the operation that maintains capacity for that rule.","unsure":""}
{"id":17,"explanation":"Call _flush before closing _sink. Closing drops _buf, so reversing the order could lose buffered data.","unsure":""}
{"id":18,"explanation":"The request-supplied userPath must resolve within workspaceRoot; reject paths using .. that escape it. The resolve and normalize expression is the code this requirement applies to.","unsure":""}
{"id":19,"explanation":"Drain the ring before freeing buf. Otherwise an interrupt handler could still use buf after it has been freed. #2201 is an issue reference.","unsure":""}
{"id":20,"explanation":"Reserve space for n items here to get one allocation; growing through push_back accounted for 40% of the measured profile. doc:perf-notes#ingest points to the ingest section of the performance notes.","unsure":""}
{"id":21,"explanation":"Use HOLDLOCK on this SQL Server MERGE because concurrent upserts can race without it. doc:mssql-merge#concurrency points to the concurrency guidance.","unsure":""}
{"id":22,"explanation":"Use an autonomous transaction for the audit operation so its row survives if the caller rolls back its own transaction.","unsure":""}
{"id":23,"explanation":"SQLite's ALTER TABLE cannot drop the needed constraint directly, so the migration rebuilds the table, beginning with leases_new. doc:sqlite-alter#otheralter points to the relevant ALTER TABLE documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":24,"explanation":"Poll every five seconds instead of relying on inotify because the NFS mounts in question emit no inotify events.","unsure":""}
{"id":25,"explanation":"Keep the awaited run calls in a for...of loop. Putting await inside forEach would let errors escape the intended try/catch handling.","unsure":""}
{"id":26,"explanation":"The Vec<u8> returned by read_frame must have a length no greater than MAX_FRAME. The decoder enforces this by rejecting larger frames.","unsure":""}
{"id":27,"explanation":"Register drainHook before pool.start() so a SIGTERM shutdown can drain the pool, including if termination occurs after startup begins.","unsure":""}
{"id":28,"explanation":"Move the retry policy out of this hard-coded backoff and into configuration. The task is complete when Default in internal/retry/policy.go reads that configuration; the path and symbol identify the target code.","unsure":""}
{"id":29,"explanation":"Issue #412 contains the full matrix of allowed lease state transitions for Active, Released and Stale.","unsure":""}
{"id":30,"explanation":"Pass the token to tool login only through standard input, as the command does with --token-stdin. Do not put it in command arguments, because other users can see arguments through ps.","unsure":""}
{"id":31,"explanation":"Create the app_reader role before granting it SELECT access. Migration 042 assumes that role already exists.","unsure":""}
{"id":32,"explanation":"Make on_event idempotent because Stripe may retry the same webhook for three days. doc:stripe#webhook-retries points to the webhook retry documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":33,"explanation":"Compare the supplied and expected MACs with hmac.Equal to use a constant-time comparison. Using == would expose timing information.","unsure":""}
{"id":34,"explanation":"Build CodeGraph once per index, at a cost proportional to the number of edges. Do not rebuild it for each query.","unsure":""}
{"id":35,"explanation":"Changing the packed TCustomerRec layout would make existing saved .dat files incompatible. Bump FILE_VERSION if the layout changes.","unsure":""}
{"id":36,"explanation":"Change MSG_MAX together with MSG_MAX_WIRE in proto/messages.h. The path and symbol identify the related wire-size limit.","unsure":""}
{"id":37,"explanation":"When handler runs after authMiddleware, session.userId must be non-null. Code in this handler relies on that authentication invariant.","unsure":""}
{"id":38,"explanation":"Synchronize access to cache because the check followed by put must be one atomic operation. A ConcurrentHashMap alone would not make those separate steps atomic.","unsure":""}
{"id":39,"explanation":"The repository alias comes from a user, so validate it against the registry before joining it into a path. #1996 is an issue reference for this security requirement.","unsure":""}
{"id":40,"explanation":"Payment Amount must be non-negative. Refunds are represented as separate rows whose Kind is 'R', rather than as negative amounts in this insert.","unsure":""}
{"id":41,"explanation":"Set stop_ before joining worker_. Otherwise the worker may never exit and join would block forever.","unsure":""}
{"id":42,"explanation":"The limiter is sized around the external GitHub API allowance of 5,000 requests per hour per token. doc:github-rest#rate-limits points to the rate-limit documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":43,"explanation":"Stop the cidx service before replacing its binary. Replacing the binary while it is running can fail with 'Text file busy'.","unsure":""}
{"id":44,"explanation":"Do not share the _lease field across jobs belonging to different users; doing so could expose one user's credentials to another. #77 is an issue reference.","unsure":""}
{"id":45,"explanation":"Ensure ids contains no more than 999 values before binding it to this DELETE statement, because the stated SQLite limit is 999 bound variables per statement.","unsure":""}
{"id":46,"explanation":"If cgroup creation fails because the memory containment setup cannot be established, log the error and let the job continue. The code deliberately avoids aborting the job on that failure.","unsure":"The comment says 'containment failure' but does not specify whether cgroup creation can fail for reasons other than a bad memory estimate."}
{"id":47,"explanation":"Remove the legacy /v1/jobs route. #530 is the issue tracking that removal.","unsure":""}
{"id":48,"explanation":"doc:adr-007#session-model points to the session-model section of architecture decision record 007, which explains why SessionRegistry keeps sessions per tab.","unsure":""}
{"id":49,"explanation":"This partial index includes only leases with released_at IS NULL, making active-lease lookups 30 times faster according to the noted measurement.","unsure":""}
{"id":50,"explanation":"Keep EVENT_TYPES synchronized with EVENT_LABELS in web/src/events.ts and with docs/events.md. Those paths identify the related code and documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":51,"explanation":"Sweep must not evict a bucket merely because it has been idle longer than IdleTTL. It also checks fullAt so an evicted key cannot return before its scheduled refill and incorrectly receive a fresh bucket. TestSweepKeepsBucketsThatWouldNotBeFullYet is the test for this behavior.","unsure":""}
{"id":52,"explanation":"Allow a request when tokens is at least 1-eps because fractional refill calculations can drift slightly below 1. Requiring exactly 1 would deny a request that has effectively earned a token. TestFractionalRefillIsPreservedAcrossRequests covers this.","unsure":""}
{"id":53,"explanation":"The insert's RETURNING clause is expected to produce a row, so this code uses a double TypeScript cast to treat get's result as TransferRow rather than adding a null check.","unsure":""}
{"id":54,"explanation":"After enabling foreign keys, query sqlite_schema to force SQLite to read the database schema. The comment says PRAGMAs alone do not read the file, so this query causes openDb to reject a file that is not a database.","unsure":""}
{"id":55,"explanation":"Keep the guarded set_int_max_str_digits(0) call. On CPython 3.9.14 and later, removing it can cause a ValueError when processing integers longer than 4,300 digits.","unsure":""}
{"id":56,"explanation":"Keep the 'equity' literal in this trigger synchronized with EQUITY_ACCOUNT in src/ledger.ts. The path and symbol identify the matching account definition.","unsure":""}
{"id":57,"explanation":"Check isApplied again inside the transaction's write lock, even though the migration appeared in the earlier pending scan. Another migrator could have applied it meanwhile; the second check prevents applying it twice.","unsure":""}
